{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>On the day of your slaughter it shall be eaten.</b> It is a commandment to eat it on the first day itself, and on the next day it is likewise permitted to eat it if anything remains from the first day. This is the meaning of שלמים being eaten for two days and one night — the night being the middle night between the two days, for the night after the two days is not subject to eating, because it is נותר, and it is also not burned until morning, because the burning takes place by day. And this is what it says: ״והנותר ממנו עד יום השלישי באש תשרף״ — it does not come to permit eating at night, but only that the burning shall be by day."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:26:42.872076639Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}